# File-system rules

## No backup or temp files in the main tree

The main editable app tree is `_______KDB3/KDB3/` (CSS, JS, HTML/templates, assets for the redesign).

Forbidden under `_______KDB3/KDB3/`:

- `*_old.*`, `*_backup.*`, `*_v1.*`, `*_v2.*`, `*_temp.*`, `*_copy.*`
- Files with `.bak`, `.tmp`, `.orig`, `.save` extensions
- Suffix-renamed duplicates of any kind

A file you want to delete is deleted, not renamed with a suffix.

## "Keep for reference" code

- Code worth keeping for reference does NOT live under `_______KDB3/KDB3/`.
- Move it to `_______KDB3/humanDocs/` (human-only; AI read/write rules per `ai-discipline.mdc`). Use a subfolder such as `humanDocs/notes/` if you want a dedicated scratch area.
- Reference snippets in briefs/docs should be inline citations (path + line range), not duplicated files.

## `architecture/` is not a dump tree

- `_______KDB3/architecture/` holds only the **catalog** files (`filesExplained.md`, `eventSubscribe.md`, … per `architecture.mdc`). Do not place backup copies, forks, or “old version” source files there.

## Deletes are real deletes

- When a file is no longer used, delete it.
- Do not leave orphaned files "in case".
- The git-loze nature of the project makes orphans dangerous: nobody knows whether they are still wired up.
